00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:26.000
And you have interviewed a number of mass shooters personally, right? I mean, how did you go about that? How did you find them and convince them to talk to you? Why would they talk to you? Yeah. So before I went to graduate school, before I was an academic, I worked with men facing the death penalty as an investigator, and I developed their cycle, social life histories for their sentencing hearings.
你曾亲自采访过几位大规模枪击者，对吧？我的意思是，你是怎么做到的？你是如何找到他们并说服他们跟你谈话的？他们为什么会跟你谈话？是的。所以在上研究生之前，在我成为学者之前，我作为一名调查员与面临死刑的男性合作过，我为他们的量刑听证会撰写了他们的社会心理生平史。

42
00:27:26.000 --> 00:28:13.000
And so to me, it wasn't that big of a stretch to just say, well, let's just go talk to them, right? Like, let's go ask them why they did it. And people looked at me like I was out of my mind. But we, I just wrote a letter to every living perpetrator I could find who was incarcerated, incarcerated for life. Most of them die in the act like we talked about. Most of them either killed themselves or are killed. So we identified, I want to say, 32 maybe, who were a living. I sent just, you know, letters, cold letters saying that I was a researcher and I wanted to talk to them. I didn't want to talk about their crime. I only wanted to talk about the build up to the crime and what their life was like up to the
所以对我来说，只是去和他们谈谈并不是什么大跨越，对吧？就像，让我们去问问他们为什么要这样做。人们看我的眼神就像我疯了一样。但是，我只是给我能找到的每一个被监禁的、被判终身监禁的在世凶手写了一封信。正如我们所讨论的，他们大多在行动中死亡。他们大多要么自杀，要么被杀。所以我们确定了，我想说大约32名仍在世的凶手。我只是发出，你知道的，冷信，说我是一名研究人员，我想和他们谈谈。我不想谈论他们的罪行。我只想谈谈犯罪之前的积蓄过程，以及他们在犯罪之前的

43
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:38.000
crime. I said you weren't going to get paid. I would never use your name. You weren't going to get any fame or attention out of this. The goal of this project is to prevent mass shootings in the future. And I got, well, I got a number of responses. I got some attorneys who said they can't because they're in a piece. heels. I got two very angry kind of I hate psychologists. Don't contact me. But I got seven perpetrators
生活是什么样的。我说你不会得到报酬。我永远不会使用你的名字。你不会从中获得任何名誉或关注。这个项目的目标是预防未来的大规模枪击事件。我得到了，嗯，我得到了一些回应。我有几位律师说他们不能接受，因为他们正在上诉。我有两个非常愤怒的、类似于“我恨心理学家，别联系我”的回应。但我得到了七个凶手的回应，

